content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage requires corrective action: the manual directs mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No allowable leakage-rate limit is stated. P2 is appropriate for planned repair because the reported readings do not meet the documented immediate-stop or temperature-triggered P1 criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 3.9 mm/s falls within Figure 3 Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation', provided the report is confirmed as RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing. It is above the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary but below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C 'Restricted - plan maintenance' boundary and the 7.1 mm/s Zone D boundary. Because the site stop rule applies to the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, the reported value does not require an immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature: 71 C is 1 C above the documented normal maximum of 70 C, but below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits. Bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface. The site requirement for a priority-1 work order applies when temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit; 71 C does not meet that trigger, but the above-normal temperature requires investigation of grease quantity, bearings and alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn, cracked or early-failed mechanical seal faces are the leading explanation for the shaft-seal leakage. For serial HF3-22000 specifically, the bulletin documents early failure of HF3-450 component seals caused by a revised sleeve tolerance; confirm whether that seal is currently fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible seal dry-running or loss of flush: dry running is a documented cause of seal leakage, and this pump uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry. No dry-running event is reported, so this remains a hypothesis to check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a common documented cause across seal leakage, vibration and elevated bearing temperature; check it rather than assuming the seal alone caused all symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing or bearing wear could explain the above-normal housing temperature. Check grease quantity and bearing condition before deciding whether bearing replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, complete electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and drain and vent under a line-break permit. Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-105 is on the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Arrange the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment, then remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly. The back pull-out design permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, and withdraw the existing seal and sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the removed seal for worn or cracked faces and evidence of dry-running, and inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring. Investigate the Plan 11 flush arrangement and alignment as possible causes. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check bearing grease quantity and inspect the bearings. If either bearing shows wear, noise or a high-temperature condition requiring bearing replacement, replace drive-end bearing HF3-512 and non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 together as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial. No sleeve measurement is needed to set the pre-set cartridge, but the sleeve-scoring inspection and replacement criterion still apply. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with lightly oiled threads and tighten: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm; HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm; and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check and correct shaft alignment using a laser alignment tool; laser alignment is mandatory after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning to service, restore the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and do not run the seal dry. Resume the specified monitoring: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and measure bearing temperature on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one; mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above. Do not fit HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; install new with the seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve: supply one only if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Conditional drive-end bearing 6312-C3; required only if bearing-pair replacement is confirmed, and must be replaced together with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Conditional non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; required only if bearing-pair replacement is confirmed, and must be replaced together with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Any work inside the pump or on its seal requires electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-105 is within P-101 to P-106 on the chemically dosed filtered-water line, which contains sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-rule threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current readings do not trigger an immediate stop. If subsequent vibration is classified in Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Planned mechanical-seal replacement: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Planned laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement, only if inspection establishes the need: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians for the bearing pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-105 is exactly serial HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B must be used. Pumps below this serial remain on the manual arrangement and are not relevant to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, while the applicable bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Use 30 Nm for this asset's cartridge seal. The other applicable Table 5 torques remain unchanged.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Procedure difference: the manual describes component-seal removal and sleeve inspection, whereas the bulletin states that HF3-450B is pre-set and needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting. For this asset, omit the cartridge-setting sleeve measurement but retain the scoring inspection and replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 3.9 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and which housing was measured? Only one reading is supplied, although monitoring requires both housings and classification of the highest reading (C06, C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, HF3-450 or HF3-450B, and has SB-2026-014 already been implemented? This determines whether the documented HF3-450 early-failure mode applies, although any replacement on this serial must be HF3-450B (C13).",
    "Is there any history of seal-flush loss or dry-running, and what is the observed leakage rate? Dry-running is a documented possible cause, but the evidence supplies neither the operating history nor an allowable leakage-rate threshold (C02, C09).",
    "Do bearing inspection, noise, grease condition and alignment checks confirm a need for bearing-pair replacement? The 71 C reading is above normal but below alarm, and no bearing inspection results are supplied (C02, C09, C10).",
    "Does shaft-sleeve scoring exceed 0.1 mm depth? The replacement of HF3-455 is conditional on that inspection result (C13)."
  ]
}
